
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt PIPRO 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pipro
.Nd profile command pipelines
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h | Fl -help
.Op Fl s | Fl -static
.Op Fl q | Fl -quiet
.Op Fl d Ar decimals | Fl -decimals Ar decimals
.Ar pipeline
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
executes a pipeline of commands and reports resource usage and timing
information for each process in the pipeline.
It is intended to help identify performance bottlenecks and failures
without requiring each command to be run individually.
.Pp
The pipeline must be supplied as a single argument.
Commands are separated by the
.Sq |
character.
.Nm
is not a shell, and does not support all shell syntax.
.Pp
For each process,
.Nm
reports its wall-clock runtime, user CPU time, system CPU time,
exit status, and peak memory usage.
The precision and availability of these measurements may vary by
operating system.
.Pp
When standard output is connected to a terminal,
.Nm
displays a live progress interface unless static output is requested.
Otherwise, it prints a static report.
The output produced by the final command in the pipeline is displayed
after execution unless quiet mode is enabled.
.Sh OPTIONS
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Display usage information and exit.
.It Fl s , Fl -static
Disable the live progress interface and print a static report.
ANSI escape sequences are stripped from the report.
.It Fl q , Fl -quiet
Suppress the captured output of the pipeline.
.It Fl d Ar decimals , Fl -decimals Ar decimals
Set the number of decimal places displayed for supported measurements.
Not all measurements can provide meaningful precision at the
requested level.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Profile a simple pipeline:
.Pp
.Dl pipro 'cat file.txt | grep example | wc -l'
.Pp
Print a static report with four decimal places:
.Pp
.Dl pipro -s -d 4 'cat file.txt | grep example | wc -l'
.Pp
Suppress the output:
.Pp
.Dl pipro -q 'cat file.txt | grep example | wc -l'
.Sh CAVEATS
.Nm
does not implement a complete shell parser.
Shell features such as redirection and complex quoting are not fully
supported.
.Pp
Resource usage measurements depend on the facilities provided by the
underlying operating system.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An volatilespectre
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sh 1 ,
.Xr time 1,
.Xr pipe 2
